### Minecraft Modding ###
run/
!**/src/**/run/
# The Symbol Chat compatibility run: a game directory of its own, so the mods Connector needs are
# never mixed into the ordinary run.
run-symbolchat/
# The CIT Resewn and RP Renames compatibility run, for the same reason: Fabric mods loaded through
# Connector, and the patcher that keeps them working there, downloaded into a game directory of their
# own rather than into the ordinary run.
run-citresewn/
# The dedicated test server's game directory, for the same reason and one more: a server and a client
# cannot share a game directory at all, and what a server writes there - the world, its logs, the
# databases under serverconfig - has no business in the repository.
run-server/
**/src/generated/**/.cache/
repo/
!**/src/**/repo/

### Runtime output ###
# The game logs into run/logs; anything at the root is from a stray run.
logs/
